# Analects Book 13 (子路) — draft, first half: lemmata 0–24 = passages 13.1–13.14. Token format as the pilot:
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every bound compound and every character not yet in the glossary (on every occurrence).
# Passages follow Zhu Xi's chapter breaks (凡三十章): 13.1 = units 0–1, 13.2 = 2–3, 13.3 = 4–10, 13.4 = 11–13,
# 13.5 = 14, 13.6 + 13.7 = 15, 13.8 = 16, 13.9 = 17–20, 13.10 = 21, 13.11 = 22, 13.12 = 23, 13.13 + 13.14 = 24.
# Units 15 and 24 each hold TWO of Zhu Xi's chapters, which the edition prints with only a ○ between and no
# comment: pas="13.6" npas=2 and pas="13.13" npas=2 (the card shows "6–7", "13–14"); the second chapter
# starts a new verse line, and the note says so.
# Quotation marks balance within every unit. Where a speech runs on past one of Zhu Xi's comments (13.3 units
# 8–10 after 7, the Master; 13.4 unit 13 after 12, the Master) the continuation is left unquoted, Chinese and
# English alike (as Books 8–12). Quotes inside a quote: 『』 in w, ‘’ in l and i (16 Prince Jing's sayings;
# 22 the old saying the Master quotes, Zhu Xi 古有是言而夫子稱之).
# Repeats (shipped English reused): 無倦 'do not weary' (1; cf. 12.14 居之無倦 'without wearying');
# 衛君 'the lord of Wei', unbound (4; as 7.14); 必也…乎 'If it must be anything, it would be…' (5; as 12.13);
# 闕 'leave aside' (7; as 2.18); 禮樂 'the rites and music', 樂 yuè, unbound (9; as 11.1); 焉用 'what use
# (is there for)' (13; as 5.5, 12.19); 詩三百 'the Odes, three hundred' (14; as 2.2); 於従政乎何有 'in
# government, what trouble would he have?' / i 'what would hold him back in government?' (24; as 6.6);
# 如…何 'what of…?' (24; as 4.13); 退朝 'came back from court', 朝 cháo (24; as 10.12).
# Readings decided:
#   勞 láo (0; Zhu Xi 如字 = the plain reading, not lào 'to encourage', noted); 為 wéi throughout (2 'to serve
#   as', 4 為政, 11 為圃, 14 奚以為 final, 22 為邦); 焉 yān 'how/what' (3, 13; 於䖍反); 知 zhī (3 ×3, 7);
#   舍 shě (3; 上聲); 將 jiāng (4); 由 yóu 'Yóu' (7, as Book 11); 葢 gài (7); 闕 quē (7); 樂 yuè (9 ×2);
#   興 xīng (9 ×2); 中 zhòng 'to hit the mark' (9 ×2; 去聲); 行 xíng (10 'carry out', 15 'get done');
#   好 hào (13 ×3; 去聲); 夫 fú (13; 音扶); 襁 qiǎng (13; Zhu Xi 居丈反 = jiǎng, noted); 使 shǐ (14; Zhu Xi
#   去聲 shì, noted); 弟 dì in 兄弟 (15); 従 cóng (15, 24); 少 shǎo 'a little (more)' (16); 合 hé, 完 wán (16);
#   適 shì (17); 僕 pú (17); 教 jiào (20); 期 jī (21; Zhu Xi 周一嵗之月); 勝 shèng and 去 qù (22; Zhu Xi
#   勝平聲 shēng, 去上聲 qǔ, noted); 殺 shā (22); 殘 cán (22); 世 shì (23); 朝 cháo (24; 音潮);
#   與 yù 'to take part in' (24; 去聲).
# Glyphs kept as printed: 葢 (7), 従 (15, 24), 荆 (16). (逺 occurs only in Zhu Xi's comments in this half.)
# Bound (keys exist): 子路, 仲弓, 季氏, 有司, 君子, 樊遲, 小人, 兄弟, 冉有, 善人, 冉子.
# New bound keys needed:
#   樊須 (fán xū — Fan Xu: Fan Chi's personal name, used by the Master in 13.4; Zhu Xi gives no gloss here)
#   四方 (sì fāng — the four quarters: every direction, the states round about (四方之民 13.4, 使於四方 13.5);
#         bound as 四海 was in Book 12)
#   公子荆 (gōng zǐ jīng — Prince Jing of Wei, a duke's son and grandee of Wei; Zhu Xi: 公子荆衛大夫; Wang Su
#         in He Yan counts him with 蘧瑗 and 史鰌 among the gentlemen of Wei). 衛 stays a separate token, as
